WEBVTT

00:01:20.780 --> 00:01:22.160
STUDENT ID
MICHIRU KAGEMORI

00:01:48.560 --> 00:01:50.980
I passed the audition!

00:01:51.060 --> 00:01:52.150
That's great!

00:01:52.230 --> 00:01:54.320
I knew you could do it, Nazuna!
Keep it up!

00:01:56.740 --> 00:01:57.700
Nazuna?

00:02:18.420 --> 00:02:22.600
ANIMA-CITY OFFICIAL WEBSITE

00:02:23.810 --> 00:02:25.970
<i>Dear Mom and Dad,</i>

00:02:26.560 --> 00:02:31.230
<i>I would rather live in Anima-City</i>
<i>than be cooped up in my room.</i>

00:02:31.810 --> 00:02:34.360
<i>Please don't worry about me. Michiru.</i>

00:02:47.200 --> 00:02:48.540
Good morning, Jem!

00:02:49.040 --> 00:02:50.290
It's a nice day, isn't it?

00:02:50.370 --> 00:02:52.040
How do you like that room?

00:02:52.130 --> 00:02:53.920
It's nicer on the roof, isn't it?

00:02:54.420 --> 00:02:56.090
Yes, it is. Thank you.

00:02:57.880 --> 00:03:01.010
Jem, what's that big building over there?

00:03:02.390 --> 00:03:03.800
Oh, the Medi-Cen.

00:03:04.430 --> 00:03:06.560
That's Sylvasta Medical Center.

00:03:06.640 --> 00:03:11.060
It's a research center and hospital
run by Sylvasta Pharmaceutical.

00:03:11.140 --> 00:03:12.770
Sylvasta?

00:03:13.400 --> 00:03:16.480
Oh, maybe they can help me
with my disease.

00:03:26.410 --> 00:03:29.250
Hey! What do you think you're doing?

00:03:29.330 --> 00:03:30.750
Why, you!

00:03:30.830 --> 00:03:35.170
Why won't it open? Hey!
What's going on? Let me out of here!

00:03:35.290 --> 00:03:37.840
-Hey! Come on!
-Keep quiet.

00:03:37.920 --> 00:03:39.090
It won't open!

00:03:39.170 --> 00:03:40.010
STUDENT ID

00:03:40.090 --> 00:03:41.800
I realize you're human now.

00:03:42.180 --> 00:03:43.550
Then why are you doing this?

00:03:43.640 --> 00:03:45.260
Your very existence is dangerous.

00:03:45.350 --> 00:03:47.260
What? How could it be?

00:03:47.640 --> 00:03:51.480
If humans find out they might turn
into beastmen, it'll cause panic.

00:03:51.890 --> 00:03:54.190
Don't come out
until we find out more information.

00:03:54.600 --> 00:03:55.980
I'll bring you food.

00:03:56.060 --> 00:03:59.030
What? Are you insane? This makes no sense!

00:03:59.110 --> 00:04:02.570
Trust me. I will protect the peace
for all beastmen.

00:04:02.650 --> 00:04:05.570
Trying to sound cool
doesn't make me trust you!

00:04:05.660 --> 00:04:07.030
It just sounds creepy!

00:04:08.080 --> 00:04:11.370
Open up! I'm going to that hospital!

00:04:11.450 --> 00:04:12.330
No.

00:04:14.540 --> 00:04:17.090
If you set a single foot outside,
I'll kill you.

00:04:17.670 --> 00:04:20.090
So my peace means nothing?

00:04:22.630 --> 00:04:24.720
Rearranging furniture so early
in the morning?

00:04:24.800 --> 00:04:25.800
It must be rough.

00:04:26.640 --> 00:04:27.640
Mayor.

00:04:28.220 --> 00:04:30.010
The mayor?

00:04:31.720 --> 00:04:33.430
-A bombing?
-That's right.

00:04:33.850 --> 00:04:36.810
The director of Sylvasta Medical Center

00:04:36.900 --> 00:04:39.860
reported to the police
that they'd received a threat.

00:04:39.940 --> 00:04:41.110
Then early this morning,

00:04:41.190 --> 00:04:44.320
<i>a truck carrying Sylvasta drugs</i>
<i>was blown up.</i>

00:04:44.400 --> 00:04:45.820
A bombing?

00:04:47.070 --> 00:04:48.410
Now my ears?

00:04:48.990 --> 00:04:49.830
Whatever.

00:04:50.290 --> 00:04:54.710
"If you've got money to build a hospital
and buy cutting-edge devices for beastmen,

00:04:54.790 --> 00:04:56.500
then use it for humans."

00:04:57.000 --> 00:04:58.840
Those are the bomber's demands.

00:04:58.920 --> 00:05:01.050
Are those anti-beastman lowlifes
behind this again?

00:05:01.500 --> 00:05:04.590
The police tried to trace the scent
of the bomb,

00:05:04.670 --> 00:05:07.720
but the explosion erased the scent,

00:05:07.800 --> 00:05:10.140
they couldn't find any leads.

00:05:10.560 --> 00:05:13.100
That superb sense of smell
of yours would be

00:05:13.180 --> 00:05:15.640
more use than the police investigators.

00:05:16.020 --> 00:05:18.230
Please find the bomb.

00:05:19.520 --> 00:05:21.610
There are patients in the Medi-Cen.

00:05:22.110 --> 00:05:23.230
There's no time to lose.

00:05:24.440 --> 00:05:28.870
If the hospital's blown up,
my disease may never get cured!

00:05:28.950 --> 00:05:30.490
Holy crap! Holy freaking crap!

00:05:32.080 --> 00:05:35.000
Help me, Mayor!

00:05:35.830 --> 00:05:37.080
I just heard someone.

00:05:37.710 --> 00:05:38.710
I didn't.

00:05:40.250 --> 00:05:44.210
Help me! I'm being held prisoner!

00:05:47.010 --> 00:05:47.930
That's Kuro.

00:05:48.340 --> 00:05:49.800
He's learned to mimic.

00:05:53.930 --> 00:05:54.770
Move those.

00:05:58.190 --> 00:05:59.440
Ogami!

00:06:01.560 --> 00:06:04.730
Mayor, this man's a woman kidnapper!

00:06:04.820 --> 00:06:07.320
-Hey!
-He said he'd kill me if I left!

00:06:07.400 --> 00:06:09.030
He's also a blackmailer!

00:06:09.110 --> 00:06:11.450
It was to protect you and all beastmen.

00:06:12.410 --> 00:06:14.540
So you're Michiru Kagemori.

00:06:15.450 --> 00:06:17.910
Just looking at you,
I see you're obviously a beastman.

00:06:18.370 --> 00:06:21.170
I find it hard to believe
that you used to be a human.

00:06:22.290 --> 00:06:23.500
You knew about her?

00:06:23.590 --> 00:06:26.510
I need to know everything
about Anima-City.

00:06:26.590 --> 00:06:28.170
That's the job of a mayor.

00:06:28.630 --> 00:06:31.090
I see. It was Grand Grandma.

00:06:31.180 --> 00:06:33.890
A mayor also needs to protect her sources.

00:06:34.350 --> 00:06:35.390
Well...

00:06:35.970 --> 00:06:38.940
please let me help find the bomb.

00:06:39.770 --> 00:06:40.690
Why?

00:06:40.770 --> 00:06:44.110
Sylvasta Pharmaceutical
has cutting-edge devices, right?

00:06:45.110 --> 00:06:47.900
Then maybe they can cure my disease.

00:06:48.490 --> 00:06:49.950
Who says it's a disease?

00:06:50.450 --> 00:06:52.950
But it's true that she was once a human.

00:06:53.450 --> 00:06:55.660
There's still a chance
it could be a disease.

00:06:56.080 --> 00:06:58.330
It's not safe to let her out though.

00:06:58.790 --> 00:07:02.790
If anti-beastmen humans find out
about her, who knows what will happen?

00:07:02.880 --> 00:07:04.290
I'm not sitting still!

00:07:05.710 --> 00:07:09.260
Before I got here,
I just sat around holding my breath.

00:07:09.670 --> 00:07:11.380
I was cooped up in my room.

00:07:11.840 --> 00:07:14.680
After I ran off,
I had to avoid beastman hunters

00:07:14.760 --> 00:07:16.970
to finally make it to this city.

00:07:17.060 --> 00:07:20.520
But now I have to hide again?
There is no way I am doing that!

00:07:20.600 --> 00:07:21.520
Now, you listen.

00:07:24.560 --> 00:07:28.230
We're shorthanded. Let's have her help us.

00:07:29.030 --> 00:07:31.240
She can communicate for Kuro.

00:07:32.990 --> 00:07:34.570
Communicate for Kuro?

00:07:34.660 --> 00:07:38.200
Just looking at her,
you can't tell she used to be a human.

00:07:38.580 --> 00:07:41.290
Going around Anima-City
shouldn't be a problem.

00:07:42.000 --> 00:07:46.210
However, don't mention to anyone else
that you used to be a human.

00:07:46.590 --> 00:07:47.590
All right.

00:07:48.000 --> 00:07:51.010
Can you forget about
being kidnapped and threatened?

00:07:52.430 --> 00:07:53.430
Fine.

00:07:54.090 --> 00:07:55.090
Then have this.

00:07:56.180 --> 00:07:58.810
A mobile phone! It's been so long!

00:07:58.890 --> 00:08:01.980
If Kuro finds anything, contact Ogami.

00:08:02.390 --> 00:08:05.310
This is a fragment of the bomb
found at the scene.

00:08:08.480 --> 00:08:12.030
Sylvasta Pharmaceutical
is part of the Sylvasta conglomerate,

00:08:12.110 --> 00:08:13.950
a prominent wealthy family.

00:08:14.740 --> 00:08:16.280
They support what the mayor says

00:08:16.370 --> 00:08:19.290
about "equal rights for beastmen
and humans alike."

00:08:19.740 --> 00:08:22.250
They also provide massive funding
for Anima-City.

00:08:22.660 --> 00:08:24.580
Lots of humans can't stand that.

00:08:25.370 --> 00:08:28.040
But there are rumors
that Sylvasta Pharmaceutical

00:08:28.130 --> 00:08:30.050
is profiting from beastman data.

00:08:30.800 --> 00:08:33.840
Not all beastmen are happy
to have them around.

00:08:34.510 --> 00:08:36.760
Then why did you accept this job?

00:08:38.140 --> 00:08:41.060
I thought you only did stuff for beastmen.

00:08:41.770 --> 00:08:43.890
I can't refuse the mayor.

00:08:43.980 --> 00:08:44.810
Is that so?

00:09:04.500 --> 00:09:07.120
Ogami here. I've located the bombs.

00:09:07.830 --> 00:09:09.880
<i>There are six bombs in total.</i>

00:09:09.960 --> 00:09:11.630
<i>Send the bomb squad.</i>

00:09:12.000 --> 00:09:14.760
-You go to Medi-Cen.
-There's one at Medi-Cen too?

00:09:15.130 --> 00:09:18.720
No. There's no scent of a bomb there.
This is just in case.

00:09:18.800 --> 00:09:22.430
The bomber's real target is Sylvasta,
after all.

00:09:23.350 --> 00:09:24.890
Wait! I'm going with you!

00:09:25.600 --> 00:09:27.350
There are six bombs in total.

00:09:27.440 --> 00:09:28.600
-Let's move it!
-Yes, sir!

00:09:50.380 --> 00:09:51.290
Kuro?

00:09:53.000 --> 00:09:53.840
Wait for me!

00:10:03.600 --> 00:10:04.890
Hurry it up!

00:10:04.970 --> 00:10:06.430
Chill out.

00:10:06.520 --> 00:10:10.400
The cops are too busy
dealing with the bomb threat.

00:10:10.480 --> 00:10:12.650
At any rate, this is the last time!

00:10:13.150 --> 00:10:17.610
Gosh, why so cold? You've profited plenty
from this as well, you know.

00:10:17.700 --> 00:10:19.030
"Profited plenty"?

00:10:19.610 --> 00:10:21.160
What's that all about?

00:10:25.580 --> 00:10:28.160
Hey! I see you eavesdropping over there!

00:10:29.040 --> 00:10:29.870
Darn it!

00:10:29.960 --> 00:10:32.340
Who's there? Show yourself!

00:10:37.260 --> 00:10:38.170
Get her!

00:10:40.840 --> 00:10:43.390
She saw us!
She could have heard something too!

00:10:43.470 --> 00:10:46.430
You think I'd let a little girl
like that get away?

00:10:48.100 --> 00:10:51.190
Hold on. I think I've seen her face
somewhere before.

00:10:54.360 --> 00:10:55.820
Would you answer the phone?

00:10:57.940 --> 00:10:59.860
Good. That's the last one.

00:11:07.200 --> 00:11:09.080
-It's her!
-"Her"?

00:11:13.170 --> 00:11:14.170
That's her!

00:11:16.090 --> 00:11:17.460
She's that girl!

00:11:22.720 --> 00:11:25.890
So what were you doing back there,
you little brat?

00:11:26.350 --> 00:11:29.180
I just got a little lost.

00:11:29.640 --> 00:11:33.230
Oh, really? Are you sure
you didn't overhear anything important?

00:11:35.940 --> 00:11:39.860
What a bad-mannered kid you are.
We need to teach you some manners.

00:11:44.870 --> 00:11:45.910
Cut it out.

00:11:45.990 --> 00:11:47.370
It's Ogami!

00:11:48.660 --> 00:11:50.330
-Why, you!
-I'll kill you!

00:11:54.210 --> 00:11:56.210
Scram. I won't kill you.

00:11:57.000 --> 00:11:58.000
Not today, at least.

00:11:59.550 --> 00:12:00.970
I'll get you for this!

00:12:01.340 --> 00:12:02.970
I'm glad I made it in time.

00:12:03.050 --> 00:12:04.590
Kuro told me.

00:12:04.680 --> 00:12:06.930
Damn you! I called you multiple times.

00:12:07.510 --> 00:12:10.060
Sorry. Why did those guys come after you?

00:12:10.850 --> 00:12:11.890
I don't know.

00:12:11.980 --> 00:12:15.900
Maybe because I saw some suspicious guys
loading stuff behind Medi-Cen?

00:12:16.400 --> 00:12:18.020
Who were those guys?

00:12:18.110 --> 00:12:19.070
They're a gang.

00:12:19.150 --> 00:12:20.320
A gang?

00:12:20.820 --> 00:12:23.740
They work with Medi-Cen employees
to divert goods.

00:12:27.160 --> 00:12:27.990
An explosion?

00:12:30.620 --> 00:12:32.290
You stay at the Beast Co-op!

00:12:32.370 --> 00:12:34.960
No way! I don't want this place
to get blown to bits!

00:12:35.040 --> 00:12:35.960
It's dangerous!

00:12:37.040 --> 00:12:38.210
Fine. I accept it.

00:12:40.170 --> 00:12:41.880
I'm actually a human.

00:12:42.340 --> 00:12:44.340
But right now, I'm a beastman.

00:12:45.180 --> 00:12:46.890
What are you talking about?

00:12:46.970 --> 00:12:49.350
You protect all beastmen, right?

00:12:50.970 --> 00:12:52.770
Then protect me too.

00:12:53.730 --> 00:12:55.390
I'm a beastman, after all.

00:12:58.190 --> 00:12:59.360
You're such a pain.

00:13:08.570 --> 00:13:09.660
How awful.

00:13:11.330 --> 00:13:12.290
Ogami.

00:13:12.790 --> 00:13:15.460
This is Mr. Yaba,
the Medical Center director.

00:13:17.420 --> 00:13:19.670
This is the work of those bombers too.

00:13:20.250 --> 00:13:23.050
The police will pay
for not preventing this!

00:13:24.510 --> 00:13:26.260
Allow me to investigate as well.

00:13:26.840 --> 00:13:29.970
He's an advisor
who helps with our investigations.

00:13:30.550 --> 00:13:31.600
May he?

00:13:32.520 --> 00:13:33.640
Fine. Do as you like.

00:13:39.650 --> 00:13:42.150
I find it hard to believe
Ogami missed this one.

00:13:43.110 --> 00:13:45.820
I traced that bomb fragment perfectly.

00:13:46.320 --> 00:13:47.700
So how did I miss this?

00:13:59.460 --> 00:14:00.460
That's it!

00:14:02.380 --> 00:14:03.710
Did you figure it out?

00:14:04.630 --> 00:14:05.760
There's no scent.

00:14:08.380 --> 00:14:12.220
-Mimura, that girl is back!
-You're kidding!

00:14:13.100 --> 00:14:14.220
We have no choice.

00:14:15.020 --> 00:14:16.100
Right.

00:14:20.150 --> 00:14:21.440
<i>Chairman?</i>

00:14:22.020 --> 00:14:24.150
I heard the Medi-Cen was bombed.

00:14:24.610 --> 00:14:25.990
What a frightful world.

00:14:26.070 --> 00:14:27.240
<i>That's right.</i>

00:14:27.320 --> 00:14:30.280
<i>The research center's</i>
<i>Data Management Department was bombed.</i>

00:14:30.360 --> 00:14:34.830
<i>But since the hospital's data</i>
<i>was kept elsewhere, it's safe.</i>

00:14:35.370 --> 00:14:37.200
I see. That's good news.

00:14:37.910 --> 00:14:39.830
<i>Repair the facility immediately.</i>

00:14:40.330 --> 00:14:42.040
<i>Spare no expense.</i>

00:14:42.460 --> 00:14:45.670
<i>Make sure there's no evidence</i>
<i>of the terrible disaster.</i>

00:14:46.420 --> 00:14:48.670
<i>Not a single trace, Mr. Yaba.</i>

00:14:49.170 --> 00:14:50.090
Yes, sir.

00:14:51.720 --> 00:14:54.350
Unbelievable. What a lot of trouble.

00:14:56.350 --> 00:14:57.390
Director Yaba.

00:14:58.350 --> 00:15:00.480
Can we speak to you?

00:15:00.980 --> 00:15:02.480
What do you want now?

00:15:02.560 --> 00:15:05.190
I demand you take responsibility for this!

00:15:07.030 --> 00:15:12.320
We examined the site of the explosion,
but couldn't pick up the culprit's scent.

00:15:12.410 --> 00:15:13.780
Are you making excuses?

00:15:14.240 --> 00:15:15.490
Not just the culprit.

00:15:15.990 --> 00:15:18.370
There's no scent at all
at the scene for a time.

00:15:18.450 --> 00:15:19.830
That doesn't happen.

00:15:20.410 --> 00:15:23.460
The scent doesn't just
completely disappear.

00:15:24.170 --> 00:15:27.710
Not unless a special chemical is used
to eliminate all odors.

00:15:28.800 --> 00:15:31.590
<i>Mr. Yaba,</i>
<i>you could develop a chemical like that</i>

00:15:31.680 --> 00:15:33.970
<i>at this research center, couldn't you?</i>

00:15:34.050 --> 00:15:35.640
Don't be ludicrous!

00:15:35.720 --> 00:15:38.600
How dare you accuse me
to hide your own incompetence?

00:15:39.060 --> 00:15:42.600
I saw your employee
doing a deal with gangsters!

00:15:42.980 --> 00:15:45.310
I bet you're involved in that.

00:15:45.400 --> 00:15:49.820
You faked the bombings and blew up
the research center to cover that up.

00:15:50.240 --> 00:15:53.280
Hold on! How can you trust
what this guy says?

00:15:57.330 --> 00:15:59.660
<i>When I trace the scent left</i>
<i>at a crime scene,</i>

00:15:59.750 --> 00:16:01.410
<i>I always find the culprit.</i>

00:16:02.620 --> 00:16:05.630
<i>That's because all beastmen carry a scent.</i>

00:16:06.460 --> 00:16:08.590
<i>But at this crime scene,</i>

00:16:08.670 --> 00:16:12.090
<i>there was a time and location</i>
<i>where there was no scent at all.</i>

00:16:12.760 --> 00:16:16.550
And there's been no scent
on either of your hands...

00:16:17.550 --> 00:16:20.470
ever since the explosion
at this research center.

00:16:25.020 --> 00:16:27.900
In accordance with the regulations
of the Beastmen Special Zone,

00:16:27.980 --> 00:16:31.110
the analysis of the whiff
will be used as proof.

00:16:32.990 --> 00:16:36.870
Mr. Yaba, why don't you give me
your story down at the station?

00:16:43.580 --> 00:16:44.790
Shirou!

00:16:45.710 --> 00:16:46.960
Don't move!

00:16:47.040 --> 00:16:49.290
If you do, I'll strangle the girl!

00:16:53.050 --> 00:16:54.340
Run, Mimura!

00:16:57.680 --> 00:16:58.680
After them!

00:16:58.760 --> 00:16:59.680
Okay.

00:17:11.690 --> 00:17:14.360
Your claws are no match for my skin!

00:17:14.450 --> 00:17:18.120
You faked a disaster
to save your own skin.

00:17:18.200 --> 00:17:21.330
My bare hands are enough
for a coward like you!

00:17:29.080 --> 00:17:33.800
For a beastman who has abandoned
his pride, this horn is meaningless!

00:17:33.880 --> 00:17:35.510
Don't! Please, don't!

00:17:35.590 --> 00:17:37.890
Not my horn! Anything but my horn!

00:17:46.520 --> 00:17:49.100
-Let the girl go!
-Don't move!

00:17:49.520 --> 00:17:51.860
Move an inch, and I'll drop her!

00:17:52.360 --> 00:17:54.990
You'll never get away by doing this!

00:17:55.070 --> 00:17:56.490
It's all your fault!

00:17:56.570 --> 00:18:00.530
If it hadn't been for you,
we never would have had all this trouble!

00:18:01.410 --> 00:18:02.790
If you don't want her to die,

00:18:03.240 --> 00:18:05.750
get me 100 million yen
and a helicopter for my escape!

00:18:06.210 --> 00:18:07.250
Don't be ridiculous!

00:18:14.000 --> 00:18:15.130
Kuro!

00:18:15.210 --> 00:18:17.670
Don't try to get past
a chameleon's blind spot.

00:18:17.760 --> 00:18:21.970
If you pull anything else, I'll kill her!
Get me the money and the helicopter!

00:18:22.430 --> 00:18:24.640
<i>This guy is serious.</i>

00:18:28.730 --> 00:18:31.230
<i>If only my arms could stretch like before.</i>

00:19:10.310 --> 00:19:11.730
Shirou!

00:19:12.810 --> 00:19:13.980
I'm alive.

00:19:14.520 --> 00:19:15.820
Can you get off me?

00:19:20.740 --> 00:19:21.990
Ogami!

00:19:22.070 --> 00:19:25.280
You shouldn't move around.
Get checked out at Medi-Cen.

00:19:25.700 --> 00:19:27.290
No. I'm fine.

00:19:29.200 --> 00:19:30.620
Can you walk?

00:19:30.710 --> 00:19:32.710
-Yes.
-Good grief.

00:19:34.130 --> 00:19:35.790
Are you sure you're all right?

00:19:35.880 --> 00:19:37.210
I won't die.

00:19:39.420 --> 00:19:42.470
Well, thanks for saving me.

00:19:43.090 --> 00:19:46.220
I promised, didn't I?
I will protect all beastmen.

00:19:50.640 --> 00:19:52.730
<i>Yaba and Mimura confessed.</i>

00:19:52.810 --> 00:19:55.560
They conspired to embezzle.

00:19:56.230 --> 00:19:58.730
They realized
that the executives had noticed,

00:19:58.820 --> 00:20:01.200
so they blew up
Medi-Cen's database system.

00:20:01.650 --> 00:20:05.410
<i>They hired criminals</i>
<i>to play the part of bombers</i>

00:20:05.490 --> 00:20:08.580
and planned to destroy the evidence
of their embezzlement.

00:20:09.080 --> 00:20:11.410
-Was that really all it was?
-What do you mean?

00:20:12.330 --> 00:20:14.500
It seemed like the malice

00:20:14.580 --> 00:20:16.670
of that Mimura guy
was more intense than that.

00:20:17.250 --> 00:20:19.300
If it hadn't been for you...

00:20:19.380 --> 00:20:24.050
Why would they have blown up their own
research center to protect themselves?

00:20:24.550 --> 00:20:29.510
Adults are always trying to hide things
that make them look bad.

00:20:29.600 --> 00:20:32.180
-Are you talking about me?
-Who knows?

00:20:33.230 --> 00:20:35.900
I'm sorry. I won't lock you up again.

00:20:37.940 --> 00:20:40.150
You were so firm about it before!

00:20:40.570 --> 00:20:42.490
I don't want to be compared to that scum.

00:20:43.110 --> 00:20:45.860
But don't you dare tell anyone
about that beastman disease.

00:20:46.320 --> 00:20:47.410
I know.

00:20:47.490 --> 00:20:50.950
Michiru, I'll look into finding a cure
for you too.

00:20:52.200 --> 00:20:55.000
She's a leading
beastman genetic researcher.

00:20:55.710 --> 00:20:58.040
She is the first beastman
to get a doctorate degree.

00:20:58.460 --> 00:21:00.550
I'm a politician now though.

00:21:01.000 --> 00:21:05.010
My research is also what brought me
and Sylvasta Pharmaceutical together.

00:21:05.430 --> 00:21:08.760
That's how we got their support
for the establishment of Anima-City.

00:21:09.220 --> 00:21:10.640
Is that so?

00:21:10.720 --> 00:21:13.230
Be careful of Sylvasta Pharmaceutical.

00:21:13.310 --> 00:21:14.810
They're pretty fishy.

00:21:14.890 --> 00:21:15.730
How come?

00:21:16.100 --> 00:21:19.310
No reason. It's just that my nose says so.

00:21:20.650 --> 00:21:22.320
You mean, your feral instincts?

00:21:22.730 --> 00:21:24.780
Are you making fun of me?

00:21:25.400 --> 00:21:26.320
Not in the least.

00:21:31.240 --> 00:21:34.750
You guys, your research here is done.

00:21:35.120 --> 00:21:36.580
We're being transferred?

00:21:36.670 --> 00:21:38.710
Yes. I'm going with you.

00:21:39.500 --> 00:21:43.420
Why don't we see with our own eyes
what the beastman home is like?

00:21:44.460 --> 00:21:47.180
It's been ten years since Anima-City
was established, right?

00:21:47.590 --> 00:21:49.680
This will be an important juncture.

00:22:48.490 --> 00:22:50.490
Subtitle translation by Brian Athey
